#!/bin/sh
#
# The gate that runs before anything leaves this machine.
#
# One line on purpose: the list lives in a root script, so the hook and a human
# typing the same command run the same thing and neither can drift. The doctor
# asserts this file stays a delegation and does not grow its own list again.
#
# `check:fast` rather than `check`, and the difference is where the slow half
# went rather than whether it runs. The doctor, the formatter and the types take
# seconds; the browser tests and the screenshot freshness take minutes, and CI
# runs every one of them on the push this hook just allowed. Paying for both
# meant paying twice for the same answer, and the one that arrived first was the
# one blocking the person who had already finished the work.
#
# Both are turbo graphs now rather than `&&` chains, which changed the arithmetic
# twice over: the checks run beside each other instead of in sequence, and a
# repeat with nothing changed replays from cache in well under a second. The
# reason to keep the split is no longer the seconds - it is that a browser test
# needs a build, and a build is the one thing worth not doing twice.
#
# Skip deliberately with `git push --no-verify` - a hook you cannot bypass is a
# hook people delete.

pnpm run check:fast
